course: dictionary
lesson: 15798
title: Unasked: not asked
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The prefix un- often means not. «Happy» means feeling good, so «unhappy» means not happy. Unasked is built the same way: un- plus asked means not asked.
explain: «Mum gave me some unasked advice about my homework.» Nobody had asked her for advice, so she gave it without being asked. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Mum gave me some not-asked advice" still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: Unasked can also mean without being invited. «Ben came to the picnic unasked.» Nobody invited Ben, so he came without anyone asking him to. Read the words around the word, and they will tell you which meaning fits.
fact: Unasked means not asked.
fact: «An unasked question» is one that nobody has asked yet.
fact: «Unasked-for advice» is advice given without anyone asking for it.
fact: «Unasked» can also mean without being invited, as in «he came to the party unasked».
fact: Unasked-for help can be kind or annoying, depending on how it is given.
exercise: «Mum gave me some unasked advice about my homework.» What does unasked mean here? | Asked for twice | Written down neatly | Very loud | *Not asked for
exercise: «Lily arrived at the party unasked.» What does unasked mean here? | Very happy | Dressed in red | *Not invited | Late for school
exercise: What does the un- in unasked tell you? | Before | Very big | *Not | Again
test: «The class still had an unasked question about the sum.» What is an unasked question? | A very long question | *A question nobody has asked yet | A question about sums only | A question that has been answered
test: «Dad's unasked-for help with my bike was kind, but I did not need it.» What is unasked-for help? | Help you asked for twice | Help from a bike shop | Help that is always rude | *Help given without anyone asking for it
exam: «Ben came to the picnic unasked, so nobody had invited him.» What does unasked mean in this sentence? | Very tired | Late | *Not invited | Hungry
